Package: cosmobot
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ca-certificates, podman, uidmap, passt, dbus-user-session, bubblewrap, python3, git, tree
Recommends: fuse-overlayfs
Suggests: emacs-nox, typst
Description: extensible AI bot for chat platforms
 Platform-neutral agent runtime with Matrix, Telegram, QQ, Discord,
 and RPC interfaces, sandboxed tools, and persistent conversations.

Package: cosmobot-plugin-sdk
Section: haskell
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: cabal-install, ghc (>= 9.6)
Description: Cabal source SDK for developing cosmobot plugins
 Haskell declarations and a JSON-RPC runtime for standalone plugins.
 Includes sources, an example, tests, and the plugin protocol guide.
 Add /usr/share/cosmobot-plugin-sdk to the packages in cabal.project.
 Cabal builds the SDK with the plugin's compiler and dependencies.

Package: python3-cosmobot-plugin
Section: python
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Python SDK for developing cosmobot plugins
 Async handlers, typed tool schemas, and a JSON-RPC runtime for standalone
 cosmobot plugins. Import cosmobot_plugin to declare commands and tools.

Package: cosmoscope
Section: web
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: nginx | caddy | httpd
Description: static web interface for cosmobot
 Browser interface for chat, configuration, and administration over RPC.
 Static files are installed in /usr/share/cosmoscope. Configure a web server
 to serve that directory; no Node.js runtime is required.
